<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Dividing surds and simplifying into the form k*sqrt(m)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: Write <code>16*sqrt(2)</code> to represent \(16\sqrt{2}\).)</i></p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} \]</p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Divide the numbers outside the square roots</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@p@} \div {@q@} = {@r@}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Divide the square roots using \(\dfrac{\sqrt{a}}{\sqrt{b}} = \sqrt{\dfrac{a}{b}}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{\sqrt{{@m@}}} = \sqrt{\frac{{@nm@}}{{@m@}}} = \sqrt{{@n@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Combine the outside number and the simplified root</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} = {@r@} \times \sqrt{{@n@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
